# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#169-g), E §10 l.472 and R1 (L §8): explain of a field read of an adjusted instance prints the rows
# its value reads, v1's; v2's row, known after the booking cut, is read by the adjustment's re-measurement only.
# 2.1.7's refcore listed v2:amt[2026-02] too. T's fixes/g5/p4_adj_e2.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input amt[m in months]: money PLN question "Ile?"
input dom: int
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt[m]

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 10 "s"
  amt[2026-01..2026-02] = 100.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-01
  amt[2026-02] = 200.00 PLN "s"

ask a1: pay[2026-02].cash.amount
ask e2: explain pay[2026-02].cash.amount
=== expect
a1: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
e2: 100.00 PLN
  [1] row v1:dom = 10
      version v1, source s, "s", locator "s", governs 2026-01-01.., known 2026-01-01
  [2] row v1:amt[2026-01..2026-02] = 100.00 PLN
      version v1, source s, "s", locator "s", governs 2026-01-01.., known 2026-01-01
  cut 2026-06-30
